-- Section 2023: Reading Passage 3: Invasion of the Robot Umpires
INSERT INTO sections (id, test_id, type, title, instructions, audio_url, passage_text, order_index) VALUES
(2023, 202, 'reading', 'Reading Passage 3: Invasion of the Robot Umpires', '<div class="ielts-reading-container"><h2 class="ielts-reading-question-section-heading">
                                            Questions 27-32                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                    </h2>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-question-section-content">
                                            <p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage?</p>
<p>In boxes on your answer sheet, write</p>
<p><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer</p>
<p><strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer</p>
<p><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-questions">
                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="27"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">27</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>When DeJesus first used ABS, he shared decision-making about strikes with it.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="27" name="question_27" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="27" name="question_27" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="27" name="question_27" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="28"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">28</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>MLB considered it necessary to amend the size of the strike zone when criticisms were received from players.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="28" name="question_28" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="28" name="question_28" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="28" name="question_28" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="29"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">29</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>MLB is keen to justify the money spent on improving the accuracy of ABS’s calculations.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="29" name="question_29" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="29" name="question_29" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="29" name="question_29" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="30"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">30</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>The hundred-mile-an-hour fastball led to a more exciting style of play.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="30" name="question_30" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="30" name="question_30" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="30" name="question_30" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="31"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">31</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>The differing proposals for alterations to the baseball bat led to fierce debate on Sword’s team.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="31" name="question_31" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="31" name="question_31" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="31" name="question_31" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="32"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">32</strong><span class="ielts-q-title"><span>ABS makes changes to the shape of the strike zone feasible.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="32" name="question_32" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="32" name="question_32" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="32" name="question_32" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div></div>
                                                                                                                                    </div>
                                                                                                                                                            <h2 class="ielts-reading-question-section-heading">
                                            Questions 33-37                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                    </h2>
                                        <div class="ielts-reading-question-section-content">
                                            <div class="ielts-reading-section-content-wrapper"><p>Complete the summary using the list ofphrases, <strong>A-H,</strong> below.</p>
<p>Write the correct letter, <strong>A-H</strong>, in boxes on your answer sheet.</p>
<p><strong>Calls by the umpire</strong></p>
<p>Even after ABS was developed, MLB still wanted human umpires to shout out decisions as they had in their <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">33</strong><select data-qnum="33" name="question_33" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 33 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. pitch boundary">A. pitch boundary</option><option value="B. numerous disputes">B. numerous disputes</option><option value="C. team tactics">C. team tactics</option><option value="D. subjective assessment">D. subjective assessment</option><option value="E. widespread approval">E. widespread approval</option><option value="F. former roles">F. former roles</option><option value="G. total silence">G. total silence</option><option value="H. perceived area">H. perceived area</option></select></span></span>. The umpire’s job had, at one time, required a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">34</strong><select data-qnum="34" name="question_34" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 34 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. pitch boundary">A. pitch boundary</option><option value="B. numerous disputes">B. numerous disputes</option><option value="C. team tactics">C. team tactics</option><option value="D. subjective assessment">D. subjective assessment</option><option value="E. widespread approval">E. widespread approval</option><option value="F. former roles">F. former roles</option><option value="G. total silence">G. total silence</option><option value="H. perceived area">H. perceived area</option></select></span></span> about whether a ball was a strike. A ball is considered a strike when the batter does not hit it and it crosses through a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">35</strong><select data-qnum="35" name="question_35" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 35 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. pitch boundary">A. pitch boundary</option><option value="B. numerous disputes">B. numerous disputes</option><option value="C. team tactics">C. team tactics</option><option value="D. subjective assessment">D. subjective assessment</option><option value="E. widespread approval">E. widespread approval</option><option value="F. former roles">F. former roles</option><option value="G. total silence">G. total silence</option><option value="H. perceived area">H. perceived area</option></select></span></span> extending approximately from the batter’s knee to his chest.</p>
<p>In the past, <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">36</strong><select data-qnum="36" name="question_36" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 36 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. pitch boundary">A. pitch boundary</option><option value="B. numerous disputes">B. numerous disputes</option><option value="C. team tactics">C. team tactics</option><option value="D. subjective assessment">D. subjective assessment</option><option value="E. widespread approval">E. widespread approval</option><option value="F. former roles">F. former roles</option><option value="G. total silence">G. total silence</option><option value="H. perceived area">H. perceived area</option></select></span></span> over strike calls were not uncommon, but today everyone accepts the complete ban on pushing or shoving the umpire. One difference, however, is that during the first game DeJesus used ABS, strike calls were met with <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">37</strong><select data-qnum="37" name="question_37" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 37 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. pitch boundary">A. pitch boundary</option><option value="B. numerous disputes">B. numerous disputes</option><option value="C. team tactics">C. team tactics</option><option value="D. subjective assessment">D. subjective assessment</option><option value="E. widespread approval">E. widespread approval</option><option value="F. former roles">F. former roles</option><option value="G. total silence">G. total silence</option><option value="H. perceived area">H. perceived area</option></select></span></span></p>
</div>                                                <div class="options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--inline" data-dnd-group="1597045">
